sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-glue-11> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "Evolutionary changes in ion channel properties that lead to genetic assimilation of bioelectrically induced phenotypes are likely an important aspect of the evolution of body plans and other morphological features, analogous to the Baldwin effect for learning.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Genetic assimilation of bioelectric phenotypes likely shaped body-plan evolution";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Levin M, “Bioelectric networks: the cognitive glue enabling evolutionary scaling from physiology to mind”, Animal cognition (2023), doi:10.1007/s10071-023-01780-3; section “Basal cognition without neurons: what dynamic bodies think about › Re-writing morphogenetic memories: ontogenetic and evolutionary timescales”. Scope: Evolution of animal body plans"
}
